Add meson option for Geul common headers directory

The NXP meson.build files read COMMON_HEADERS_DIR from the environment via
run_command('sh', '-c', 'echo $VAR'). Meson does not reliably propagate the
environment to run_command() during cross configuration, which silently
disables the geul_ipc and baseband/la12xx drivers.

Add a proper meson option, falling back to the environment variable to keep
compatibility with the original NXP build flow.

Signed-off-by: <Julien Moucadel>

diff --git a/drivers/baseband/la12xx/meson.build b/drivers/baseband/la12xx/meson.build
index 9884edf..1dc324c 100644
--- a/drivers/baseband/la12xx/meson.build
+++ b/drivers/baseband/la12xx/meson.build
@@ -9,8 +9,11 @@ sources = files('bbdev_la12xx.c', 'bbdev_la12xx_feca_param.c', 'bbdev_la12xx_wdo
 cflags += ['-DHOST=1',
            '-DMODEM=0']
 
-cmd = run_command('sh', '-c', 'echo $COMMON_HEADERS_DIR')
-COMMON_HEADERS_DIR = cmd.stdout().strip()
+COMMON_HEADERS_DIR = get_option('common_headers_dir')
+if COMMON_HEADERS_DIR == ''
+	cmd = run_command('sh', '-c', 'echo $COMMON_HEADERS_DIR', check: false)
+	COMMON_HEADERS_DIR = cmd.stdout().strip()
+endif
 message('COMMON_HEADERS_DIR=' + COMMON_HEADERS_DIR)
 includes += [include_directories(COMMON_HEADERS_DIR)]
 
